Defects found:

- Line 150, check CANNOT FAIL / status wrapper: input file `x_REVIEW.html` containing `<script>fetch("https://api.openalex.org/works")</script>`, run `python scripts/external_dependency_census.py --repo DIR --glob x_REVIEW.html`; consequence: dependency is detected and printed, but process exits `0`, so a CI gate cannot fail.

- Line 57, selector misses corpus form: input `<script src="https://cdnjs.cloudflare.com/ajax/libs/x.js"></script>`; consequence: external code loaded by the page is invisible to `hosts_in_scripts()` because only the tag body is scanned, not `src`.

- Line 48, selector keyed too narrowly: input `<script>fetch("//api.openalex.org/works")</script>`; consequence: a browser-valid third-party request is missed because only `http://` / `https://` literals match.

- Line 73, tabulation/count collision: input files `a/page_REVIEW.html` and `b/page_REVIEW.html`, both with dependency hosts, using `--glob **/*_REVIEW.html`; consequence: `flagged[os.path.basename(p)]` collapses both to `page_REVIEW.html`, undercounting affected pages.

- Lines 90 and 92, selector keyed to wrong string: input page making `fetch("https://notlocalhost.example/x")`; consequence: a third-party request is suppressed because the filter rejects any URL containing the substring `localhost`, not just the local origin.

- Line 128, zero conflated with absent corpus: input `--glob NO_MATCHES.html`; consequence: `n == 0` causes `ZeroDivisionError` instead of reporting an empty/no-corpus condition.

COULD NOT DETERMINE different-copy defect: missing the server/caller contract proving `localhost:--port` serves exactly `--repo`.

No proven defect found for: probe keyed to string a fix removes; idempotency guard satisfied by own comment; CRLF/LF text comparison; negation dropped.
